.TH WSH-SUN-PROMS 1 "" "wsh-lab" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wsh-sun-proms \- install Sun boot PROM images you are entitled to use, from a source you provide
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wsh-sun-proms install \-\-source
.I SRC
.RB [ \-\-type " dir|archive|git|http]"
.RB [ \-\-ref
.IR REF ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RI [ NAME " ...]"
.br
.B wsh-sun-proms status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B wsh-sun-proms verify
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ NAME " ...]"
.br
.B wsh-sun-proms remove
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RI [ NAME " ...]"
.PP
Each command also takes
.BI \-\-dir " DIR" ,
.BI \-\-manifest " FILE"
and
.BI \-\-state " FILE" .
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wsh-sun-proms
copies Sun boot PROM images from a source you provide into the directory QEMU loads firmware from,
.I /usr/share/kvm
by default, under the names the sparc32 profiles of qemu-server and the PVE UI use
.RB ( "bios: ss5.bin" ", " ss20_v2.25_rom ", " lx.bin ).
Every file is checked against a manifest of known images (name, size, SHA-256 and the machine that
runs it,
.IR /usr/share/wsh-lab/sun-proms/manifest.json ).
No images come with the tool, and it has no default source.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Installs every known PROM found in
.I SRC
(or only the
.IR NAME s
given), mode 0644, owner root. A file is found by its name, or by its SHA-256 under any name. A file
already there with the right content is left as it is, so running it again changes nothing. A file
whose name is known but whose content differs, a name the manifest doesn't know, and a different file
already in the directory are refused unless
.BR \-\-force .
What was installed is recorded in
.I /var/lib/wsh-sun-proms/installed.tsv
(the file, its SHA-256 and the source without credentials).
.TP
.B status
Lists the known PROMs with their machine, whether each is there and matches the manifest, and where
it came from: a package (asked from dpkg), this tool (with the source and date), or neither.
.TP
.B verify
Like
.BR status ,
and exits 1 when a PROM there doesn't match the manifest, when none is there, or when one of the
.IR NAME s
(with
.BR \-\-all :
any known PROM) is missing.
.TP
.B remove
Removes the PROMs this tool installed. A file that changed since, or that the tool didn't install,
is kept unless
.BR \-\-force ;
a file that belongs to a package is always kept.
.SH SOURCES
.TP
.I a directory
searched with its subdirectories.
.TP
.I a tar or zip archive
read in memory; nothing is extracted.
.TP
.I a git repository
a URL that starts with
.BR ssh:// ,
.BR git@ ,
.B git+
or
.BR file:// ,
an https URL that ends in
.BR .git ,
a bare repository on disk, or any URL with
.BR "\-\-type git" .
It is cloned shallowly into a temporary directory with git and your own git configuration, so a
private repository works with the credentials you already use (an SSH key, a credential helper).
The clone is deleted afterwards. Needs git.
.TP
.I an https URL
of an archive, or a base URL under which each PROM is found by its name
.RI ( URL/ss5.bin ).
user:password in the URL is sent as basic authentication and not recorded. Plain http is refused
except to this host.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Where the PROMs go (default
.IR /usr/share/kvm ,
or
.BR $WSH_SUN_PROMS_DIR ).
QEMU on a PVE node only looks in
.IR /usr/share/kvm .
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest " FILE"
Another manifest (or
.BR $WSH_SUN_PROMS_MANIFEST ),
e.g. for tests.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " FILE"
Another record (or
.BR $WSH_SUN_PROMS_STATE ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ref " REF"
The branch or tag of a git source.
.TP
.B \-\-force
install: also unknown or differing files, and replace a different file. remove: also files this tool
didn't install.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run ", " \-n
Show what would change, change nothing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wsh-sun-proms install \-\-source /root/proms
wsh-sun-proms install \-\-source git@git.example.org:me/proms.git
wsh-sun-proms install \-\-source /root/proms.tar.gz lx.bin
wsh-sun-proms status
wsh-sun-proms verify \-\-all
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when something was refused, missing or doesn't match, 2 on a usage error.
.SH NOTES
A file in the directory that dpkg lists as part of a package is left to dpkg: with the right content
it counts as installed and
.B status
names the package; it is never removed, and replaced only with
.BR \-\-force .
When an upgrade drops a file from its package, dpkg deletes it: run
.B wsh-sun-proms install
again afterwards.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wsh-lab (1),
.BR qm (1)
